=== a failure's row is its block's title: its path bold, then the armed qualifier
  «r|FAIL»  «b|first»                                      «d|0.2ms» «d|(mutant armed)»
    «d|test/test_geo.ml:17»
    counterexample (case 12, shrunk 4 steps): Rect (2, 0)
    which failed at:
      «d|test/test_geo.ml:18»
      «d|expected»  «g|true»
      «d|actual»    «r|false»


=== a missing baseline qualifies the row after its duration
  FAIL  help                                       0.2ms (no baseline)
    test/test_cli.ml:9
    expect_file "test/help.expected": no baseline
    proposed (3 lines):
      + Usage: mytool [OPTIONS] COMMAND
      + Commands:
      +   run
    accept: touch 'test/help.expected' && dune runtest; dune promote test/help.expected


=== and shares the parenthesis with the armed qualifier
  FAIL  help                                       0.2ms (no baseline, mutant armed)
    test/test_cli.ml:9
    expect_file "test/help.expected": no baseline
    proposed (3 lines):
      + Usage: mytool [OPTIONS] COMMAND
      + Commands:
      +   run


=== an expected failure: XFAIL, the duration, then the reason
  XFAIL  known › broken carry                      0.2ms (expected failure: issue #42)
    test/test_carry.ml:5
    expected  1
    actual    2


=== an expected failure without a reason
  XFAIL  known › broken carry                      0.2ms (expected failure)
    test/test_carry.ml:5
    expected  1
    actual    2


=== an expected failure's block under its row, with no replay
  XFAIL  known › broken carry                      0.2ms (expected failure: issue #42)
    test/test_carry.ml:5
    counterexample (case 3): (1, 2)
    which failed with:
      carry lost


=== and styled, each line faint past its indent
  «d|XFAIL»  known › broken carry                      «d|0.2ms» «d|(expected failure: issue #42)»
    «d|test/test_carry.ml:5»
    «d|counterexample (case 3): (1, 2)»
    «d|which failed with:»
      «d|carry lost»


=== an expected failure whose message is the unexpected pass's stays excused
  XFAIL  collide                                   0.2ms (expected failure)
    expected to fail, but the test passed


=== an unexpected pass is a FAIL
  FAIL  known › fixed already                      0.2ms
    test/test_carry.ml:9
    expected to fail (issue #42), but the test passed


=== an xfail annotation on a pass changes nothing
  PASS  t                                          0.2ms

=== a passing property prints its label table
  PASS  labels visible                             1.2ms
    labels (100 passing cases):
       46.0%  even

=== and none without collected labels
  PASS  no labels                                  0.2ms

=== an expected failure's table is in its block
  XFAIL  known › broken carry                      0.2ms (expected failure: issue #42)
    test/test_carry.ml:5
    expected  1
    actual    2
    labels (100 passing cases):
       46.0%  even


=== a flaky pass names its attempts
  PASS  network › fetches the manifest             0.2ms (2 attempts)

=== a name's control bytes print escaped
  FAIL  first\x0ahalf                              0.2ms
    b


=== a skip's reason and an expected failure's stay in their rows, escaped
s: 2 tests
  SKIP  skipped (no\x0adb)
  XFAIL  excused                                   0.2ms (expected failure: issue	42)
